Changelog 0.7.2
  - removed stale occurences of old string definitions in data segment
  - For NIC optimization, merged save_windows and save_os2 into combined
    save_windows_os2 token.
  - removed obsolete Decode_Optimize_Value() function
  - renamed Print_Optimize_Read_Code() to Decode_Optimize_Value()
    which is semantically cleaner and follows the pattern of
    Decode_Modem_Value() function
  - Added new tests (17xx) to verify control flow of the input validation chain.
    New test group target is: VERIFICATION_CONTROL_FLOW
  - Added some inline documentation to `TEST.MK`
  - Replaced static `BIN\3CSEED.EXE` by runtime var `SEEDAPP` in `TEST.MK`
  - Extended `TEST.BAT` to support calling individual test targets of `TEST.MK`,
      e.g. `TEST.BAT VERIFICATION_CONTROL_FLOW`
      Without arguments, it defaults to the `smoke` target as before.
  - Removed a duplicate definition of CRLF in `3CCFGCLI.ASM`
  - Remove a code duplication in `Cfg_Dispatch_Parsed_Properties()`:
    The parser reparses pre-processed verbs `/ADAPTERNUM` and `/VERBOSE` again,
    only to skip them. While this was correct in behaviour, there's no
    point in passing them down from Pass 1 parser to Pass 2 parser.
    Instead I revised it to now only push pointers to applicable arguments
    for the `CONFIGURE` verb down.


Changelog 0.7.1:
  - Made shared NIC capability-source validity independent: unavailable
    connector or revision data no longer hides a successfully read PNP result.
    The NOPNP fixture now clears only the PNP capability bit.
  - Added shared physical NIC capability discovery.  PNP LIST and CONFIGURE
    now use EEPROM Capability bit 0 rather than the revision-level heuristic.
  - Migrated transceiver and Full Duplex capability gates and LIST reporting
    to shared live connector and derived Full Duplex capabilities.  AUTO now
    requires at least two live connector capabilities.
  - Reorganized LIST output into hardware/capability/status and configuration
    sections, including explicit connector, Full Duplex, and PNP capabilities.
  - Corrected /MODEM custom Maximum Interrupt Disable Time encodings to modify
    only EEPROM Software Information bits 13:8.
  - Added TP-only effective-transceiver validation for
    /FULLDUPLEX:ENABLED.  The undocumented EEPROM Software Information bit 15
    remains the persistent policy, while successful changes now synchronize
    and verify Window 4 Network Diagnostic bit 15 as the live hardware state.
    Synchronization also corrects a stale live state when the persistent policy
    already matches the request.
  - SAVECONFIG now splits restore commands dynamically against a 128-byte
    practical DOS batch-line budget, keeps /BADDRESS + /BSIZE atomic, and
    validates /EXECFILE as default, exact %1, or an existing literal path.


Changelog 0.7.0:
  - Corrected CONFIGURE, LIST, and SAVECONFIG Software Optimization handling
    to use EEPROM word 0Dh bits 5:4; Windows and OS/2 share its 10b value.
  - Corrected mock reset and byte-I/O protocol behavior:
    - Command-register Global Reset now fully returns the addressed adapter to
      its configuration-facing power-on-reset state, including removal of its
      active ISA decode.
    - Start Coaxial Transceiver now records only coax-start state and does not
      incorrectly assert Command-In-Progress.
    - Replaced command-only byte pairing with generic low-byte/high-byte,
      same-register, same-window, same-direction pairing; intervening
      same-adapter access invalidates an incomplete pair.
    - Removed init-time direct tag clearing.  ID initialization now performs
      the established ID-port sequence/commands, while activation and ID Global
      Reset operate from adapters currently in ID_CMD rather than host-side
      selected-tag state.
    - Made mock Nic_Get_Current_Window read and decode the emulated Status
      Register window bits, matching the REALHW backend path.
  - Centralized 3C509B hardware constants in 3C509DEF.INC.
  - Updated 3CSEED.ASM to use those shared definitions instead of duplicating
    register fields, EEPROM defaults, link-status values, and checksum ranges.
  - Corrected stale comments around EEPROM word 0Fh; seeder behavior unchanged.
  - Reworked the mock backend toward a register-accurate 3C509B device model.
    MCK v3 separates persistent EEPROM from live register and activation state.
  - Implemented EEPROM Busy polling, command/data sequencing, write enable,
    erase-before-write behavior, zero-only programming, and reset-driven
    automatic configuration reload.
  - Added Window 4 masks, ASIC revision 2 readout, physical active-IOBASE
    word-I/O dispatch, and conservative duplicate-active-IOBASE handling.
  - Reworked ISA ID-port discovery with full LFSR recognition, serial EEPROM
    reads, persisted ID states, tag selection, and deterministic wired-AND
    contention for untagged adapters.
  - Updated 3CSEED to create 3C509B-capable EEPROM images with live state and
    checksum data suitable for the hardware model.
  - Completed the Stage 1 low-level hardware-faithful mock model:
    - Implemented Window 3 Internal Configuration as live 32-bit register
      state, loaded from EEPROM words 12h/13h only during documented
      reset/automatic configuration (never continuously mirrored), and a
      minimal Window 2 live station-address register for architectural
      completeness (both currently unreachable from 3CCFGCLI).
    - Fixed ID-port FFh (Activate at preconfigured base): it is now a
      distinct command derived from the live Window 0 Address
      Configuration selector, no longer misinterpreted as E0h + selector
      1Fh.
    - Fixed ID-port Global Reset (C0h-CFh, now a proper range check) to
      broadcast the documented reset to every adapter record currently in
      MCK_ID_CMD, instead of only a single previously-selected tagged
      adapter.  Distinguished it from Command-Register Global Reset and
      from 3CCFGCLI's utility-level deactivate sequence.
    - Introduced a central Command Register decoder (Select Window, plus
      Global Reset and Start Coaxial Transceiver for architectural
      completeness; both are not presently reachable from 3CCFGCLI) shared
      by both word and byte access paths.
    - Wired the MCK v3 record's Command-In-Progress state into the Status
      Register (bit 12) with a deterministic busy-then-clear model, and
      changed Nic_Wait_Command_Ready from an unconditional success stub to
      a real poll of that state.
    - Implemented mock Nic_IO_Read_Byte/Nic_IO_Write_Byte on the same
      physical/register dispatch as word access, including Command
      Register low/high byte pairing (a low byte alone no longer executes
      a command; an unrelated adapter access invalidates a pending byte).
    - Removed the dead MCK v2 record layout (MCKR_*, MCK_CFGF_*,
      MCK_VERSION_V2) from 3C509DEF.INC now that MCK v3 fully replaced it,
      and fixed a stray MCKR_PRESENT reference in 3CSEED.ASM to MCK3R_PRESENT.
    - Documented the per-adapter/shared-bus/host-scratch classification of
      the existing ID-port scratch variables; no state was relocated, since
      the existing split (per-record contention shift registers vs. shared
      single-target state) was already correct.
    - New surfaces added in this pass (Window 2/3 registers, FFh, byte
      I/O, bytewise Command Register completion) are not yet reachable
      from any 3CCFGCLI code path, so they are not yet covered by TEST.MK;
      this is intentional scope discipline for this pass (see TODO.TXT).
      Full smoke + hardware-limit suite re-verified with no regressions.
      

Changelog 0.6.9:
  - Fixed a control-flow bug in the CONFIGURE VERBOSE reporting path where
    the OPTIMIZE-unchanged check (@@CheckOPTIMIZEUnchanged) was unreachable:
    @@CheckMODEMUnchanged always fell through to @@CheckFDUnchanged instead,
    so "Optimize mode is already configured to the requested value." could
    never be printed. The MODEM branch now correctly falls through to the
    OPTIMIZE check.
  - Fixed missing duplicate-property detection for /TR and /XCVR.
    CFG_SEEN_TR was defined but never wired into the CONFIGURE duplicate
    tracking chain, unlike every other supported property. Repeated /TR,
    repeated /XCVR, and mixed /TR + /XCVR now correctly report
    "Duplicate CONFIGURE property."
  - Confirmed (via 3C509DEF.INC and CHANGES 0.5.3) that EEPROM word 0Fh is
    the only documented checksum word; word 17h has no documented meaning.
    Removed the dead Cfg_Checksum_0F_High, Cfg_Checksum_17_Low and
    Cfg_Checksum_17_High routines in 3CCFGCLI.ASM, and the equivalent dead
    high-checksum loop (chk_high) in 3CSEED.ASM's Build_Checksum, which left
    behind an earlier, incorrect two-checksum hypothesis and had no effect
    on the generated mock state.
  - Removed the unreachable legacy 3Com command-issue procedure family in
    3CCFGCLI.ASM (Cfg_Issue_Command, Cfg_Read_Product_Revision,
    Cfg_Is_Original_3C509, Cfg_Is_Later_3C509B, Cfg_Wait_Command_Ready,
    Wait_Command_Ready), superseded by the current EEPROM transaction flow.
  - Removed unreferenced hardware-interface wrapper procedures from both
    backends (3CHWIF.ASM, 3CMOCKIF.ASM): Nic_Reg_Write_Byte (and its
    Cfg_Reg_Write_Byte helper), Nic_EEPROM_Wait_Ready,
    Nic_Scan_Active_Base_Ports, Nic_Read_Id_Contender_Data,
    Nic_Find_Duplicate_Id_Record, Nic_Read_EepromWord, Nic_Write_EepromWord.
  - Removed the unreachable 3C508 description branch and its msg_a0ac string
    from Select_Nic_Description in 3CCFGCLI.ASM; the current build only
    supports the 3C509 (9050h) product family and 3C508 is out of scope.
  - Removed 23 unreferenced diagnostic strings left over from the
    per-property INT/IOBASE/OPTIMIZE/TR echo paths that were superseded by
    the centralized transaction reporting, plus the unused EISA/MCA
    description strings (msg_a02d, msg_a02e).
  - Removed 7 write-only discovery/state variables that were never read
    after being set (id_mfr, id_factory0, id_factory1, id_factory2,
    id_sw_info, cfg_selected_index, save_revision). For id_factory0-2 and
    id_sw_info in the ID-port contention path, only the now-unused stores
    were removed; the underlying EEPROM reads were kept since they are part
    of the contention sequence. Removing save_revision also eliminates an
    unnecessary EEPROM read per exported adapter in SAVECONFIG.
  - Removed unused REALHW_BACKEND/MOCKHW_BACKEND EQU markers in 3CHWIF.ASM
    and 3CMOCKIF.ASM. MCKR_RSVD0 and the MCK_CFGF_* mock record-format
    constants are intentionally kept as documentation of the .MCK binary
    layout even though most are not yet consumed by code.
  - Added TEST.MK cases t086 (OPTIMIZE-unchanged VERBOSE message), t087
    (duplicate /TR is rejected) and t088 (mixed /TR + /XCVR duplicate is
    rejected) covering the two bug fixes above.


Changelog 0.6.8:
  - Fixed a LIST readout gap: the persistent full duplex setting was never
    displayed. LIST now emits a "Full Duplex = enabled|disabled" line,
    decoded from EEPROM_SOFTWARE_INFO (word 0Dh) bit 15. Adapters that do
    not pass the full duplex capability gate (product ID plus
    EEPROM_CAPABILITY bit 0) report "not supported", matching the gate
    already enforced by CONFIGURE /FULLDUPLEX.
  - This also repairs the standalone hardware conformance check hwc005 in
    TESTHWC.MK, which asserted on a "Full Duplex =" line that the CLI never
    produced.
  - renamed "I/O" label in `LIST` readout to "IOBASE"


Changelog 0.6.7:
  - Added a Modem Speed line to LIST, reading EEPROM_SOFTWARE_INFO bits 13:0.
  - Fixed a real-hardware conformance bug: the persistent /MODEM field is NOT
    the literal baud number. Bits 7:0 of the 14-bit field are always 20h;
    bits 13:8 hold a 6-bit count. Directly typed custom values (25-1600 step
    25) encode as (value/25)-1 in bits 13:8 (confirmed empirically: 25->20h,
    50->120h). The five named speeds (1200/2400/9600/19200/38400) are
    separate hardware-tuned constants using the same layout, not derived
    from the baud number by that formula; measured directly against the
    original utility on real hardware and recorded as EEPROM_MODEM_* in
    3C509DEF.INC. NONE is 3F20h, not zero. Cfg_Handle_MODEM, the CLI's
    verbose/echo output, LIST, and SAVECONFIG were all updated to encode and
    decode through this corrected mapping.
  - Fixed a related SAVECONFIG bug: the exported /IOBASE value was decoded
    through io_scan_table, which is only a port-probing order list, not an
    index-to-address mapping. The real encoding is linear (address =
    0200h + index*10h), matching Cfg_Prepare_IOBASE and 3CSEED.ASM. Restore
    batches previously could carry the wrong I/O base.


Changelog 0.6.6:
  - Fixed a real-hardware conformance bug: /PNP and /FULLDUPLEX now require
    ENABLED or DISABLED, matching the original 3C5X9CFG.EXE v3.2 command-line
    grammar exactly. The previous 0|1 syntax is no longer accepted.
  - SAVECONFIG now emits /PNP:ENABLED|DISABLED and
    /FULLDUPLEX:ENABLED|DISABLED so restore batches replay correctly through
    either 3CCFGCLI or the original utility via /EXECFILE.
  - Documented the /CONFIGPORT verb in README.md as an ISA ID-port relocation
    workaround from the original utility, not implemented in 3CCFGCLI.
  - Fixed another real-hardware conformance bug: disabling the Boot ROM is
    now done via /BSIZE:DISABLED, matching the original utility. /BADDRESS
    no longer accepts NONE; it only takes an address and is ignored when
    /BSIZE:DISABLED is also given. SAVECONFIG emits /BSIZE:DISABLED without
    an accompanying /BADDRESS when the Boot ROM is off.


Changelog 0.6.5:
  - Added an optional SAVECONFIG /EXECFILE:program argument that overrides the
    embedded restore program name (default: this executable), including
    literal DOS batch parameter placeholders such as %1.
  - TESTHWC.MK: use SAVECONFIG /EXECFILE:%1 for its baseline capture,
    so restore-config replays the generated batch through a configurable
    RESTOREAPP (default: the original 3Com utility)
  - Added hwc-restore-self, overriding RESTOREAPP to restore through
    3CCFGCLI itself once its own EEPROM writes are trusted.
  - Added an author attribution line and repository URL to the program banner


Changelog 0.6.4:
  - Added read-only SAVECONFIG file export for every installed adapter with an
    active I/O base. It writes one 3CCFGCLI CONFIGURE /ADAPTERNUM:N restore
    line per adapter from persistent EEPROM settings.
  - Added mock smoke coverage for SAVECONFIG output, multi-adapter export,
    /EXECFILE override, and missing-filename errors.


Changelog 0.6.3:
  - Defined the persistent Link Beat Disable policy as EEPROM Software
    Information word 0Dh bit 14. CONFIGURE /LINKBEAT remains unimplemented.
  - Fixed /MODEM read-modify-write behavior to preserve both the Link Beat
    Disable and Full Duplex bits in EEPROM word 0Dh.
  - Added NOLINKBEAT mock seeding and a regression test for MODEM preservation
    of the Link Beat Disable policy.


Changelog 0.6.2:
  - Removed obsolete mock-state LINKBEAT configuration field and flag
    definitions. The field did not map to the actual EEPROM Software
    Information Link Beat Disable bit.
  - Realigned the following mock configuration and live-register fields after
    removing the unused LINKBEAT slot. The read-only Link Status display in
    LIST remains unchanged.


Changelog 0.6.1:
  - Expanded the mock state file to a multi-record layout so the mock backend
    can enumerate and persist multiple seeded 3C509B adapters in one image.
  - Added 3CSEED ADD model [io] [irq] for appending mock NICs, with automatic
    default I/O base selection when the caller omits the base.
  - Added MULTI_NIC smoke coverage for multi-adapter LIST output,
    ADAPTERNUM-required CONFIGURE behavior, targeted adapter updates, and
    /IOBASE collision rejection against another discovered adapter.
  - Added explicit duplicate-I/O-base mock coverage to verify that a
    pre-existing conflicting seed can still migrate one selected adapter to a
    new I/O base.


Changelog 0.6.0:
  - Fixed the CLI help screen so /VERBOSE is documented correctly as a
    CONFIGURE sub-switch, and shortened its description to keep the option
    table compact and aligned.
  - Added a dedicated CLI_PARSER smoke group covering HELP output, '-' switch
    introducers, '=' value separators, and CONFIGURE with no property.
  - Added DEFAULT_NIC_SELECTION smoke coverage by cloning the core IRQ change
    tests without /ADAPTERNUM and renumbered the downstream test cases to keep
    the suite ordering coherent.
  - Added a COMBINED_TRANSACTIONS smoke group covering the highest-value shared
    CONFIGURE write paths: /IOBASE+/INT, /MODEM+/FULLDUPLEX, /IOBASE+/TR,
    /IOBASE+/BADDRESS+/BSIZE, /OPTIMIZE+/MODEM, and
    /TR:AUTO+/BADDRESS+/BSIZE on Combo adapters.


Changelog 0.5.9:
  - Centralized the release version metadata into VERSION.INC so 3CCFGCLI and
    3CSEED share the same source of truth for their banner/version output.
  - Moved the project changelog out of 3CCFGCLI.ASM into a standalone CHANGES
    file so the assembly source header stays focused on executable metadata.
  - Added explicit /IOBASE boundary coverage for the first and last valid ISA
    addresses (0200h and 03E0h), and renumbered the smoke suite to keep the
    test ordering coherent after the IOBASE block.
  - Fixed the /BADDRESS boundary-state bug caused by conflating the NONE sentinel
    with the minimum valid Boot ROM address.  The valid range remains C0000h-
    DE000h in 2000h steps, while NONE remains a distinct disabled state.
  - Clarified the smoke suite semantics and test-fail behavior in the project
    docs: the authoritative verdict is the assertion log and exit status, not an
    incidental "TEST PASS" marker.


Changelog 0.5.8:
  - Rewrote the help screen (/? /H) for readability.  Each top-level command
    (/? or /H, LIST, CONFIGURE, /VERBOSE) is now separated by a blank line.
    CONFIGURE sub-options are presented as a uniform two-column table with the
    description column aligned at position 39, using the full 80-column width
    with no line overflows.
  - /OPTIMIZE description corrected from "EEPROM optimization target" to
    "Network workload optimization" to accurately reflect its purpose.


Changelog 0.5.7:
  - Implemented /TR (/XCVR alias) CONFIGURE subverb.  Accepts TP, AUI, COAX,
    or AUTO.  Writes EEPROM_ADDR_CFG (word 08h) bits 15:14 (media selection);
    AUTO instead sets bit 7 (auto-select) and clears bits 15:14.  Shares the
    existing word 08h transaction slot with /IOBASE, /BADDRESS, and /BSIZE.
  - Product-ID capability gate: 3C509B-TP accepts TP only; 3C509B-TPC accepts
    TP and COAX; 3C509B-TPO accepts TP and AUI (no AUTO); 3C509B-Combo and
    3C509B-C accept all four values; unrecognised products are rejected.
  - Added CFG_PARSE_TR / CFG_SEEN_TR flags and CFG_ERR_TR_* error codes.
  - Updated CFG_PARSE_HW_MASK to include CFG_PARSE_TR (0400h).


Changelog 0.5.6:
  - Reordered capability gate checks ahead of the "parameter accepted" echo for
    every gated CONFIGURE verb (/PNP, /FULLDUPLEX, /BADDRESS, /BSIZE).
    Previously a request could be echoed as "accepted" and only then rejected
    once the Prepare phase ran its capability check, which read as self-
    contradictory output.  All gate checks now run in a single gate phase
    immediately after adapter selection, before any per-property echo is printed.
  - The Prepare phase for these verbs is now pure staging, since every gate has
    already passed by the time it runs.


Changelog 0.5.5:
  - Added /BADDRESS and /BSIZE CONFIGURE support, sharing EEPROM word 08h with
    /IOBASE. /BADDRESS owns bits 11:8 (Boot ROM base index), /BSIZE owns bits
    13:12 (8/16/32K).
  - Added the same TPO capability gate already used by LIST's Boot ROM decoder.
  - Widened cfg_parse_flags/cfg_seen_flags from byte to word and widened the
    commit mask so a BADDRESS/BSIZE-only change still triggers the shared
    transaction pipeline.
  - Fixed a bug in Cfg_Txn_Read_Current where the inactive-adapter /OPTIMIZE
    path was unreachable dead code.


Changelog 0.5.4:
  - Removed the unsupported LINKBEAT CONFIGURE surface after confirming that the
    original 3Com documentation describes it as a live ASIC register bit instead
    of a confirmed EEPROM field.
  - Added a read-only Link Status line to LIST, sourced from the live media
    status register.


Changelog 0.5.3:
  - Added /OPTIMIZE CONFIGURE support for DOS, WINDOWS, OS/2, and SERVER.
    The CLI stages EEPROM word 0Fh high byte, updates the shared checksum,
    and shows the stored optimization mode in LIST.


Changelog 0.5.2:
  - Added /FULLDUPLEX CONFIGURE support with boolean 0 or 1 input.
  - Fixed /MODEM preparation to preserve bit 15 while updating modem speed.
  - Added PNP capability guard: /PNP now refuses configuration on adapters that
    report no PNP support.


Changelog 0.5.1:
  - Added /MODEM CONFIGURE support with NONE plus numeric validation.


Changelog 0.5.0:
  - Added /PNP CONFIGURE support with boolean 0 or 1 input.
  - Mock state persistence now records the PNP flag consistently with EEPROM.


Changelog 0.4.1:
  - Backend split fully implemented.
  - Real hardware operations are isolated behind backend primitives in
    3CHWIF.ASM; the mock backend in 3CMOCKIF.ASM implements the same contract.
  - Mock backend behavior was aligned to real hardware semantics.


Changelong 0.4.0:
  - Preliminary backend split: real and mock interfaces are separated at compile
    time through the TASM conditional assembly symbols /dREALHW and /dMOCKHW.


Changelog 0.3.5:
  - Adds strict single occurrence validation for every supported CONFIGURE verb.


Changelog 0.3.0 - 0.3.4:
  - CONFIGURE uses one centralized staged transaction facility. /INT and /IOBASE
    handlers only parse and stage requested values, while the shared Cfg_Txn
    facility owns activation, I/O migration, EEPROM writes, checksum update,
    live register synchronization, and verification.


Compatibility note:
  - The original 3CCFG also accepted /PORT as an alias for /IOBASE. This reduced
    3CCFGCLI deliberately omits that alias. Use /IOBASE instead.


Initial Release:
  - The ISA discovery path intentionally follows the behavior recovered from the
    original 3CCFG 3.2 utility.
